msgid "asyncio and free-threaded Python"
msgstr "asyncio dan Python free-threaded"

msgid ""
"asyncio uses an event loop as a scheduler to enable highly efficient "
"concurrency by switching between tasks to allow non-blocking I/O operations. "
"This results in better performance for I/O-bound use cases. It also allows "
"off-loading CPU-bound work to a thread or process pool, but that is still "
"limited by the :term:`global interpreter lock` in CPython."
msgstr ""
"asyncio menggunakan event loop sebagai penjadwal untuk memungkinkan "
"konkurensi yang sangat efisien dengan beralih antar task agar operasi I/O "
"non-blocking dapat dilakukan. Hal ini menghasilkan kinerja yang lebih baik "
"untuk kasus penggunaan yang terikat I/O. asyncio juga memungkinkan "
"pemindahan pekerjaan yang terikat CPU ke thread atau process pool, tetapi "
"hal itu masih dibatasi oleh :term:`global interpreter lock` dalam CPython."

msgid ""
"However, in :ref:`free-threaded Python <freethreading-python-howto>`, the "
"GIL is disabled and Python can run true multi-threaded code. This means that "
"asyncio can now take advantage of multiple CPU cores without the limitations "
"imposed by the GIL."
msgstr ""
"Namun, dalam :ref:`free-threaded Python <freethreading-python-howto>`, GIL "
"dinonaktifkan dan Python dapat menjalankan kode multi-threaded yang "
"sebenarnya. Ini berarti asyncio kini dapat memanfaatkan beberapa inti CPU "
"tanpa batasan yang diberlakukan oleh GIL."

msgid ""
"Since Python 3.14, asyncio has first-class support for free-threaded Python, "
"and the implementation of asyncio is safe to use in a multi-threaded "
"environment."
msgstr ""
"Sejak Python 3.14, asyncio memiliki dukungan kelas satu untuk Python free-"
"threaded, dan implementasi asyncio aman digunakan dalam lingkungan multi-"
"threaded."

msgid ""
"A single event loop on one core can handle many connections concurrently, "
"but the Python code that runs to handle each one still executes serially. "
"Once requests involve a non-trivial amount of per-request computation, that "
"handling becomes the bottleneck, and a single core can no longer keep up. "
"Combining asyncio with threads is most useful here: by running an event loop "
"per thread, the handling of different requests can run in parallel across "
"multiple CPU cores. It is also useful when you need to run blocking or CPU-"
"bound code from an asyncio application."
msgstr ""
"Satu event loop pada satu inti dapat menangani banyak koneksi secara "
"bersamaan, tetapi kode Python yang berjalan untuk menangani masing-masing "
"koneksi tetap dieksekusi secara serial. Setelah request melibatkan komputasi "
"per-request yang tidak sepele, penanganan tersebut menjadi penghambat, dan "
"satu inti tidak lagi dapat mengimbanginya. Mengombinasikan asyncio dengan "
"thread paling berguna di sini: dengan menjalankan event loop per thread, "
"penanganan request yang berbeda dapat berjalan paralel di beberapa inti CPU. "
"Hal ini juga berguna ketika Anda perlu menjalankan kode yang memblokir atau "
"terikat CPU dari aplikasi asyncio."

msgid ""
"`Scaling asyncio on Free-Threaded Python <https://labs.quansight.org/blog/"
"scaling-asyncio-on-free-threaded-python>`__, a blog post by Kumar Aditya "
"which explains the internal changes that make asyncio safe and efficient "
"under free-threaded Python, together with benchmarks of the resulting "
"improvements."
msgstr ""
"`Scaling asyncio on Free-Threaded Python <https://labs.quansight.org/blog/"
"scaling-asyncio-on-free-threaded-python>`__, sebuah posting blog oleh Kumar "
"Aditya yang menjelaskan perubahan internal yang membuat asyncio aman dan "
"efisien di bawah Python free-threaded, beserta benchmark dari peningkatan "
"yang dihasilkan."

msgid "Thread safety considerations"
msgstr "Pertimbangan keamanan thread"

msgid ""
"While asyncio is designed to be thread-safe in a free-threaded Python "
"environment, there are still some considerations to keep in mind when using "
"asyncio with threads:"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun asyncio dirancang agar aman terhadap thread dalam lingkungan Python "
"free-threaded, masih ada beberapa hal yang perlu diingat saat menggunakan "
"asyncio dengan thread:"

msgid ""
"**Event loop**: Each thread should have its own event loop which should not "
"be shared across threads. This ensures that the event loop can manage its "
"own tasks and callbacks without interference from other threads."
msgstr ""
"**Event loop**: Setiap thread harus memiliki event loop-nya sendiri yang "
"tidak boleh dibagikan antar thread. Hal ini memastikan event loop dapat "
"mengelola task dan callback-nya sendiri tanpa gangguan dari thread lain."

msgid ""
"**Task management**: Tasks and futures created in one thread should not be "
"awaited or manipulated from another thread."
msgstr ""
"**Manajemen task**: Task dan future yang dibuat dalam satu thread tidak "
"boleh di-await atau dimanipulasi dari thread lain."

msgid ""
"**Thread-safe APIs**: When interacting with asyncio from multiple threads, "
"it's important to use thread-safe APIs provided by asyncio, such "
"as :func:`asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe` for submitting coroutines to an "
"event loop from another thread. If you need to call a callback from a "
"different thread, you can use :meth:`loop.call_soon_threadsafe` to schedule "
"it safely."
msgstr ""
"**API yang aman terhadap thread**: Saat berinteraksi dengan asyncio dari "
"beberapa thread, penting untuk menggunakan API yang aman terhadap thread "
"yang disediakan oleh asyncio, "
"seperti :func:`asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe` untuk mengirimkan coroutine "
"ke event loop dari thread lain. Jika Anda perlu memanggil callback dari "
"thread yang berbeda, Anda dapat "
"menggunakan :meth:`loop.call_soon_threadsafe` untuk menjadwalkannya dengan "
"aman."

msgid ""
"**Synchronization**: The synchronization primitives provided by asyncio "
"(like :class:`asyncio.Lock` and :class:`asyncio.Event`) are not designed to "
"be used across threads. If you need to synchronize between threads, you "
"should use the synchronization primitives from the :mod:`threading` module "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"**Sinkronisasi**: Primitif sinkronisasi yang disediakan oleh asyncio "
"(seperti :class:`asyncio.Lock` dan :class:`asyncio.Event`) tidak dirancang "
"untuk digunakan antar thread. Jika Anda perlu melakukan sinkronisasi antar "
"thread, Anda harus menggunakan primitif sinkronisasi dari "
"modul :mod:`threading` sebagai gantinya."

msgid "Using asyncio with threads"
msgstr "Menggunakan asyncio dengan thread"

msgid ""
"asyncio supports running one event loop per thread, which allows you to take "
"advantage of multiple CPU cores in a free-threaded Python environment. Each "
"thread can run its own event loop, and tasks can be scheduled on those loops "
"independently."
msgstr ""
"asyncio mendukung menjalankan satu event loop per thread, yang memungkinkan "
"Anda memanfaatkan beberapa inti CPU dalam lingkungan Python free-threaded. "
"Setiap thread dapat menjalankan event loop-nya sendiri, dan task dapat "
"dijadwalkan pada loop-loop tersebut secara independen."

msgid "Here's an example of how to use asyncio with threads::"
msgstr "Berikut contoh cara menggunakan asyncio dengan thread::"

msgid ""
"import asyncio\n"
"import threading\n"
"\n"
"async def worker(name: str) -> None:\n"
"    print(f\"Worker {name} starting\")\n"
"    await asyncio.sleep(1)\n"
"    print(f\"Worker {name} done\")\n"
"\n"
"def run_loop(name: str) -> None:\n"
"    asyncio.run(worker(name))\n"
"\n"
"threads = [\n"
"    threading.Thread(target=run_loop, args=(f\"T{i}\",))\n"
"    for i in range(4)\n"
"]\n"
"for t in threads:\n"
"    t.start()\n"
"for t in threads:\n"
"    t.join()"
msgstr ""
"import asyncio\n"
"import threading\n"
"\n"
"async def worker(name: str) -> None:\n"
"    print(f\"Worker {name} starting\")\n"
"    await asyncio.sleep(1)\n"
"    print(f\"Worker {name} done\")\n"
"\n"
"def run_loop(name: str) -> None:\n"
"    asyncio.run(worker(name))\n"
"\n"
"threads = [\n"
"    threading.Thread(target=run_loop, args=(f\"T{i}\",))\n"
"    for i in range(4)\n"
"]\n"
"for t in threads:\n"
"    t.start()\n"
"for t in threads:\n"
"    t.join()"

msgid ""
"In this example, each thread creates its own event loop "
"with :func:`asyncio.run` and runs a coroutine on it. The threads execute "
"concurrently, and in a free-threaded build they can run on separate CPU "
"cores in parallel."
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, setiap thread membuat event loop-nya sendiri "
"dengan :func:`asyncio.run` dan menjalankan coroutine di atasnya. Thread-"
"thread tersebut dieksekusi secara bersamaan, dan dalam build free-threaded "
"thread-thread tersebut dapat berjalan pada inti CPU yang terpisah secara "
"paralel."

msgid "Producer/consumer across threads"
msgstr "Producer/consumer antar thread"

msgid ""
"When a regular (non-asyncio) thread needs to hand work to an asyncio event "
"loop running in another thread, use a thread-safe primitive such "
"as :class:`queue.Queue` rather than :class:`asyncio.Queue`, which is only "
"safe within a single event loop.::"
msgstr ""
"Ketika thread biasa (non-asyncio) perlu menyerahkan pekerjaan ke event loop "
"asyncio yang berjalan di thread lain, gunakan primitif yang aman terhadap "
"thread seperti :class:`queue.Queue` daripada :class:`asyncio.Queue`, yang "
"hanya aman dalam satu event loop.::"

msgid ""
"import asyncio\n"
"import queue\n"
"import threading\n"
"\n"
"def producer(q: queue.Queue[int]) -> None:\n"
"    for i in range(5):\n"
"        print(f\"Producing {i}\")\n"
"        q.put(i)\n"
"    q.shutdown()\n"
"\n"
"async def consumer(q: queue.Queue[int]) -> None:\n"
"    while True:\n"
"        try:\n"
"            item = q.get_nowait()\n"
"        except queue.Empty:\n"
"            await asyncio.sleep(0.1)\n"
"            continue\n"
"        except queue.ShutDown:\n"
"            break\n"
"        print(f\"Consumed {item}\")\n"
"        await asyncio.sleep(item)\n"
"\n"
"q: queue.Queue[int] = queue.Queue()\n"
"consumer_thread = threading.Thread(\n"
"    target=lambda: asyncio.run(consumer(q))\n"
")\n"
"consumer_thread.start()\n"
"producer(q)\n"
"consumer_thread.join()"
msgstr ""
"import asyncio\n"
"import queue\n"
"import threading\n"
"\n"
"def producer(q: queue.Queue[int]) -> None:\n"
"    for i in range(5):\n"
"        print(f\"Producing {i}\")\n"
"        q.put(i)\n"
"    q.shutdown()\n"
"\n"
"async def consumer(q: queue.Queue[int]) -> None:\n"
"    while True:\n"
"        try:\n"
"            item = q.get_nowait()\n"
"        except queue.Empty:\n"
"            await asyncio.sleep(0.1)\n"
"            continue\n"
"        except queue.ShutDown:\n"
"            break\n"
"        print(f\"Consumed {item}\")\n"
"        await asyncio.sleep(item)\n"
"\n"
"q: queue.Queue[int] = queue.Queue()\n"
"consumer_thread = threading.Thread(\n"
"    target=lambda: asyncio.run(consumer(q))\n"
")\n"
"consumer_thread.start()\n"
"producer(q)\n"
"consumer_thread.join()"

msgid ""
"The producer runs on the main thread while the consumer runs inside an event "
"loop on its own thread, yet they communicate safely through ``queue.Queue``. "
"When the queue is empty the consumer sleeps briefly and tries again. When "
"the producer is done it calls :meth:`~queue.Queue.shutdown`, which causes "
"subsequent :meth:`~queue.Queue.get_nowait` calls to "
"raise :exc:`queue.ShutDown` so the consumer can exit cleanly."
msgstr ""
"Producer berjalan pada thread utama sementara consumer berjalan di dalam "
"event loop pada thread-nya sendiri, namun keduanya berkomunikasi dengan aman "
"melalui ``queue.Queue``. Ketika antrean kosong, consumer tidur sebentar lalu "
"mencoba lagi. Ketika producer selesai, ia "
"memanggil :meth:`~queue.Queue.shutdown`, yang menyebabkan "
"pemanggilan :meth:`~queue.Queue.get_nowait` berikutnya "
"memunculkan :exc:`queue.ShutDown` sehingga consumer dapat keluar dengan "
"bersih."
